>
> Well, probably very little. (Except nobody really knows for sure what
> a tanru is supposed to mean.)
>
> But the "poi" clause is more flexible: "lo poi broda ko'a gi'e brode
> ko'e" for example, with no "be".
>
> Or "lo poi mi djuno lo du'u ke'a mokau". Try doing that with a tanru.
>

